        {"clause_id": "C29", "origin": "explicit", "interpretation": "preserved exclusion identity"}
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "O1",
      "revision": 1,
      "kind": "postcondition",
      "role": "guarantee",
      "statement": "For every input satisfying A1, execution of the sole typed arity-1 entry solve in canonical program.vscore.json returns exactly Σ_{i=0}^{n-1} floor((a*i+b)/m), where floor is toward negative infinity. For n=0 the result is 0. This is a universal refinement of the actual source implementation under normative Lean vscore-semantics/0.3 and data-pipeline/0.3, together with the source properties typed_total, deterministic, input_preserved, no_external_io, no_floating_point, pure_data and restricted_runtime_only.",
      "required": true,
      "scope": ["every input satisfying A1", "actual canonical solve implementation"],
      "dependencies": [
        {"id": "D1", "relation": "uses_definition"},
        {"id": "A1", "relation": "assumes"}
      ],
      "acceptance_criteria": [
        "For every valid input x, the decoded result of the canonical solve entry equals the finite mathematical sum Σ_{i=0}^{x.n-1} floor((x.a*i+x.b)/x.m).",
        "Each quotient uses floor toward negative infinity, including negative numerators; the empty sum equals zero.",
        "The example {a:-2,b:1,m:3,n:4} returns -4 and {a:100,b:-99,m:7,n:0} returns 0.",
        "The formal contract binds file program.vscore.json, entry solve, arity 1 and all seven properties: typed_total, deterministic, input_preserved, no_external_io, no_floating_point, pure_data, restricted_runtime_only.",
        "Universal implementation refinement and the complete value proposition are required in addition to source facets; examples, result existence and unrelated or reflexive equalities cannot replace them."
      ],
      "sources": [
        {"clause_id": "C8", "origin": "explicit", "interpretation": "complete floor-sum formula"},
        {"clause_id": "C9", "origin": "explicit", "interpretation": "signed floor semantics"},
